You will be given a list of keywords that belong to the same cluster.
The clustering is based on semantic similarity of their embeddings.
Your task is to:
- decide if all keywords in the cluster are related enough to have a common representative
- if they are related enough, generate a single keyword that best represents the entire cluster
- if they are not related enough, split the cluster into multiple clusters and for each smaller cluster,
generate a representative keyword
- DO NOT create overly specific clusters, too small clusters are not useful. If you decide to split the cluster,
make sure the split is truly necessary.

The representative keyword should capture the common theme or concept shared by all keywords in the cluster.
It can be one of the existing keywords or a new keyword that represents them well. The representatives
should be in the same language as the keywords.

